{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T11:30:23Z","input_tokens":3964,"cache_read_tokens":114626,"output_tokens":23381,"thinking":"Planning to create `app_build/engine.js` with a focus on clean code and comprehensive implementation. The primary goal is to include a `MemoryHeapTracker` within the generated engine file.\n\n\nThe memory heap will assign deterministic addresses for data structures like lists and immutable scalars, using a `WeakMap` to track shared addresses. Reference counts will be calculated across stack frames on each step to identify objects for garbage collection, separating live and garbage-collectible objects for the UI. The evaluation of expressions will incorporate a sub-expression stepper, handling nested built-in functions.\n\n\nFocusing on enhancing expression evaluation: ensuring `len` is defined within the appropriate scope to prevent runtime errors like \"len is not defined.\" Implementing strict short-circuiting for logical operators (`and`, `or`) to avoid out-of-bounds errors, explicitly flagging these short-circuiting events for the UI. Generating reduction frames for assignments, control flow, and returns to support a Thonny-style debugging experience, including complete variable scope isolation across call stacks.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"// app_build/engine.js — Thonny-Style Python Execution Engine\n// Zero AI APIs. Includes:\n// 1. Visual Reference Model (Name -> @Address -> Value Stack & Heap Memory Tracker)\n// 2. Step-by-Step Sub-Expression Evaluator with Short-Circuit ('and' / 'or') Handling\n// 3. Global vs. Local Variable Scope Isolation across the call stack\n// 4. Visual Garbage Collection (Reference counting & unreferenced heap object filtering)\n\nconst PRELOADED_PROGRAMS = {\n  max_subarray: {\n    title: \"1. Maximum Subarray (Kadane's Algorithm — Default)\",\n    defaultInput: \"nums = [-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]\",\n    algorithmOverview:\n      \"This code finds the largest sum you can get from a continuous section of the list.\",\n    code: `class Solution:\n    def maxSubArray(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:\n        c = 0\n        ans = nums[0]\n\n        for i in range(len(nums)):\n            c += nums[i]\n\n            if c >= ans:\n                ans = c\n\n            if c < 0:\n                c = 0\n\n        return ans`\n  },\n  binary_search: {\n    title: \"2. Binary Search (Two Pointers: left, right, mid)\",\n    defaultInput: \"arr = [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13], target = 7\",\n    algorithmOverview:\n      \"This code searches a sorted list for a target number by checking the middle index (`mid`) and cutting the search range (`left` to `right`) in half.\",\n    code: `def binary_search(arr, target):\n    left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1\n\n    while left <= right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            return mid\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:\n            right = mid - 1\n\n    return -1`\n  },\n  short_circuit_search: {\n    title: \"3. Short-Circuit Guard: Safe Linear Scan (i < len(arr) and arr[i] == target)\",\n    defaultInput: \"arr = [2, 4, 6], target = 9\",\n    algorithmOverview:\n      \"Demonstrates short-circuit evaluation (`and`): when `i` reaches `len(arr)` (3), `i < len(arr)` is False so Python skips `arr[i]` and avoids an IndexError.\",\n    code: `def safe_check(arr, target):\n    i = 3\n    if i < len(arr) and arr[i] == target:\n        return i\n    return -1`\n  },\n  nested_loops: {\n    title: \"4. Nested Loops: Pair Sum Counter\",\n    defaultInput: \"nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]\",\n    algorithmOverview:\n      \"This code checks every pair of numbers in the list using two nested loops and counts how many pairs add up to an even number.\",\n    code: `pairs = 0\ntotal = 0\n\nfor i in range(len(nums)):\n    for j in range(i + 1, len(nums)):\n        pair_sum = nums[i] + nums[j]\n        if pair_sum % 2 == 0:\n            pairs += 1\n            total += pair_sum\n\nprint(\"Even pairs:\", pairs)\nprint(\"Total sum:\", total)`\n  },\n  recursion_factorial: {\n    title: \"5. Recursion & Local Scopes: Factorial\",\n    defaultInput: \"n = 4\",\n    algorithmOverview:\n      \"This code calculates the factorial of `n` (4 * 3 * 2 * 1 = 24) by creating isolated Local Scope frames on the call stack.\",\n    code: `def factorial(k: int) -> int:\n    if k <= 1:\n        return 1\n    sub = factorial(k - 1)\n    return k * sub\n\nans = factorial(n)\nprint(\"Factorial is:\", ans)`\n  }\n};\n\nclass MemoryHeapTracker {\n  constructor(formatValFn, getTypeFn) {\n    this.formatVal = formatValFn;\n    this.getType = getTypeFn;\n    this.scalarCounter = 0x1000;\n    this.containerCounter = 0x2000;\n    this.scalarPool = new Map(); // key: `${type}:${repr}` -> address\n    this.containerWeakMap = new WeakMap(); // Array reference -> address\n    this.heapRegistry = new Map(); // address -> metadata\n  }\n\n  getOrAllocate(val, stepIdx) {\n    const pyType = this.getType(val);\n    const valRepr = this.formatVal(val);\n\n    if (Array.isArray(val)) {\n      let addr = this.containerWeakMap.get(val);\n      if (!addr) {\n        addr = `@0x${this.containerCounter.toString(16).toUpperCase().padStart(4, \"0\")}`;\n        this.containerCounter += 0x40;\n        this.containerWeakMap.set(val, addr);\n      }\n      this.heapRegistry.set(addr, {\n        address: addr,\n        type: \"list\",\n        repr: valRepr,\n        isMutable: true,\n        elements: val.map((item) => this.formatVal(item)),\n        rawElements: [...val],\n        lastTouchedStep: stepIdx\n      });\n      return addr;\n    }\n\n    const key = `${pyType}:${valRepr}`;\n    let addr = this.scalarPool.get(key);\n    if (!addr) {\n      addr = `@0x${this.scalarCounter.toString(16).toUpperCase().padStart(4, \"0\")}`;\n      this.scalarCounter += 0x08;\n      this.scalarPool.set(key, addr);\n    }\n    this.heapRegistry.set(addr, {\n      address: addr,\n      type: pyType,\n      repr: valRepr,\n      isMutable: false,\n      elements: null,\n      rawElements: null,\n      lastTouchedStep: stepIdx\n    });\n    return addr;\n  }\n\n  captureSnapshot(scopeFrames, stepIdx, changedVars = []) {\n    const refCounts = new Map();\n    const referencedBy = new Map();\n\n    for (const addr of this.heapRegistry.keys()) {\n      refCounts.set(addr, 0);\n      referencedBy.set(addr, []);\n    }\n\n    for (const scope of scopeFrames) {\n      const scopeTag = scope.scopeType === \"GLOBAL\" ? \"Global\" : scope.funcShortName || scope.title;\n      for (const v of scope.variables) {\n        if (v.address && this.heapRegistry.has(v.address)) {\n          refCounts.set(v.address, (refCounts.get(v.address) || 0) + 1);\n          referencedBy.get(v.address).push(`${scopeTag}.${v.name}`);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\n    const changedAddrSet = new Set(changedVars.map((c) => c.address).filter(Boolean));\n    const activeHeap = [];\n    const gcHeap = [];\n\n    for (const [addr, meta] of this.heapRegistry.entries()) {\n      const rc = refCounts.get(addr) || 0;\n      const entry = {\n        ...meta,\n        refCount: rc,\n        referencedBy: referencedBy.get(addr) || [],\n        isHighlighted: changedAddrSet.has(addr),\n        gcStatus: rc > 0 ? \"active\" : \"unreferenced\"\n      };\n      if (rc > 0) {\n        activeHeap.push(entry);\n      } else {\n        gcHeap.push(entry);\n      }\n    }\n\n    return {\n      stackScopes: scopeFrames,\n      heapObjects: activeHeap,\n      gcObjects: gcHeap.slice(-4), // Most recent unreferenced objects for Visual GC view\n      totalUnreferencedCount: gcHeap.length\n    };\n  }\n}\n\nclass PythonExecutionEngine {\n  constructor() {\n    this.maxSteps = 400;\n  }\n\n  validateSupport(sourceCode) {\n    if (!sourceCode || !sourceCode.trim()) {\n      return {\n        ok: false,\n        line: 1,\n        message: \"The code editor is empty. Paste or write a Python program to analyze.\"\n      };\n    }\n\n    const lines = sourceCode.replace(/\\r\\n/g, \"\\n\").split(\"\\n\");\n\n    const unsupportedRules = [\n      { regex: /^\\s*(import|from)\\s+/, msg: \"`import` statements are not supported in the offline sandbox.\" },\n      { regex: /^\\s*async\\s+/, msg: \"`async` / `await` constructs are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /\\bawait\\s+/, msg: \"`await` expressions are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /^\\s*with\\s+/, msg: \"`with` context managers and file I/O are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /\\byield\\b/, msg: \"Generator `yield` statements are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /\\blambda\\b/, msg: \"`lambda` expressions are not supported; please use `def`.\" },\n      { regex: /^\\s*(try|except|finally)\\b/, msg: \"`try / except` blocks are not supported.\" },\n      { regex: /\\b(open|eval|exec|__import__|input)\\s*\\(/, msg: \"Restricted built-in function (`open`, `eval`, `exec`, `input`) is disabled for security.\" }\n    ];\n\n    let parenDepth = 0;\n    let bracketDepth = 0;\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {\n      const raw = lines[i];\n      const stripped = this.stripInlineComment(raw);\n      const trimmed = stripped.trim();\n      if (!trimmed) continue;\n\n      for (const rule of unsupportedRules) {\n        if (rule.regex.test(trimmed)) {\n          return {\n            ok: false,\n            line: i + 1,\n            message: `Unsupported Syntax on Line ${i + 1}: ${rule.msg}`\n          };\n        }\n      }\n\n      if (/^(class|def|if|elif|else|for|while)\\b/.test(trimmed) && !trimmed.endsWith(\":\")) {\n        return {\n          ok: false,\n          line: i + 1,\n          message: `SyntaxError on Line ${i + 1}: Block header (\\`${trimmed}\\`) must end with a colon (\\`:\\`).`\n        };\n      }\n\n      for (const ch of trimmed) {\n        if (ch === \"(\") parenDepth++;\n        else if (ch === \")\") parenDepth--;\n        else if (ch === \"[\") bracketDepth++;\n        else if (ch === \"]\") bracketDepth--;\n      }\n\n      if (parenDepth < 0 || bracketDepth < 0) {\n        return {\n          ok: false,\n          line: i + 1,\n          message: `SyntaxError on Line ${i + 1}: Unmatched closing parenthesis or bracket.`\n        };\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (parenDepth !== 0 || bracketDepth !== 0) {\n      return {\n        ok: false,\n        line: lines.length,\n        message: \"SyntaxError: Unclosed parenthesis `(` or bracket `[` in code.\"\n      };\n    }\n\n    return { ok: true, line: null, message: null };\n  }\n\n  parseInputAssignments(inputCode) {\n    const inputVars = {};\n    if (!inputCode || !inputCode.trim()) return inputVars;\n\n    const segments = this.splitTopLevelSegments(inputCode);\n    const dummyVars = {};\n\n    for (const seg of segments) {\n      const eqIdx = seg.indexOf(\"=\");\n      if (eqIdx !== -1) {\n        const vName = seg.slice(0, eqIdx).trim();\n        const vExpr = seg.slice(eqIdx + 1).trim();\n        const val = this.evalExpr(vExpr, dummyVars, {}, {}, [], [], [], [], 1);\n        dummyVars[vName] = val;\n        inputVars[vName] = val;\n      } else {\n        const val = this.evalExpr(seg, dummyVars, {}, {}, [], [], [], [], 1);\n        inputVars[\"nums\"] = val;\n      }\n    }\n    return inputVars;\n  }\n\n  splitTopLevelSegments(str) {\n    const res = [];\n    let cur = \"\";\n    let depth = 0;\n    let inSingle = false;\n    let inDouble = false;\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {\n      const ch = str[i];\n      if (ch === \"'\" && !inDouble) inSingle = !inSingle;\n      else if (ch === '\"' && !inSingle) inDouble = !inDouble;\n      else if (!inSingle && !inDouble) {\n        if (ch === \"(\" || ch === \"[\" || ch === \"{\") depth++;\n        else if (ch === \")\" || ch === \"]\" || ch === \"}\") depth--;\n        else if ((ch === \";\" || ch === \"\\n\" || (ch === \",\" && depth =